{"source_passage_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0002-PASSAGE", "text": "What is Posture?\n• Posture a composite of the positions of all the joints of the body at any given moment\n• Ideal posture an alignment of maximum physiological and biomechanical efficiency, which requires a minimum of stress and strain\n• Faulty posture the posture that is not an ideal posture\n(Muscles Testing and function, Kendall et\nal, 1952)", "document_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "document_title": "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "source_file": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0002"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0002", "document_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "document_title": "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "source_file": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf", "page_number": 2, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 2, "pdf_page": 2, "formatted": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf, slide 2 (PDF p. 2)"}], "slide_number": 2, "section_ids": ["HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0002", "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-PART00", "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "HHS4867-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS4867 - Functional Movement Science", "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "Postural assessment basics", "What is Posture?"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
