{"source_passage_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0025-PASSAGE", "text": "Spastic hemiplegia\n• the commonest neurological abnormal gait. It can occurs in cerebral palsy, cerebrovascular accident and traumatic brain injury.\n• A hemiplegic patient usually possesses a mixture of normal motor control, spasticity and patterned responses, he exact combination depending on the severity and location of the brain damage.\nTypical problems are as follows:\no Foot drop on the affected side\no Contracture of the calf muscles\no Overactivity of both quadriceps and\nhamstrings\no Reduced range of hip motion due to\noveractivity of ilipsaoas and the adductors", "document_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "document_title": "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "source_file": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0025"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0025", "document_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "document_title": "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "source_file": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf", "page_number": 25, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 25, "pdf_page": 25, "formatted": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf, slide 25 (PDF p. 25)"}], "slide_number": 25, "section_ids": ["HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0025", "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-PART03", "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "HHS4867-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS4867 - Functional Movement Science", "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "Pathological gait", "Spastic hemiplegia"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
