{"source_passage_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0027-PASSAGE", "text": "Spastic diplegia\nA common manifestation of cerebral\npalsy. It primarily affects the legs,\nalthough there may be considerable\nasymmetry between the two sides.\nThe commonest pattern consists of\no Hip flexion and internal rotation,\ndue to overactivity by the ilipsoas,\nrectus femoris and hip adductors.\no Knee flexion, due to overactivity of\nthe hamstrings, especially on the\nmedial side\no Equines deformity of the foot and\neversion of the hindfoot, due to\noveractivity by the triceps surae and\nperonei.", "document_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "document_title": "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "source_file": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0027"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0027", "document_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "document_title": "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "source_file": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf", "page_number": 27, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 27, "pdf_page": 27, "formatted": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf, slide 27 (PDF p. 27)"}], "slide_number": 27, "section_ids": ["HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0027", "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-PART03", "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "HHS4867-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS4867 - Functional Movement Science", "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "Pathological gait", "Spastic diplegia"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
