{"source_passage_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0029-PASSAGE", "text": "Shuffling gait\nParkinsonism\nThe commonest pattern consists of\n• Stride length and speed were very much reduces, although cycle time was usually normal\n• The walking base was slightly increased\n• The range of motion at the hip, knee and ankle were all decreased, mainly by a reduction in joint extension\n• The swinging of the arms was much reduced\n• The majority of patients rotated the trunk in phase with the pelvis instead of twisting it in the opposite direction\n• The vertical trajectories of the head, heel and toe were all reduced although other workers have commented on a distinct ‘bobbing’ motion of the head.", "document_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "document_title": "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "source_file": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0029"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0029", "document_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "document_title": "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "source_file": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf", "page_number": 29, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 29, "pdf_page": 29, "formatted": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf, slide 29 (PDF p. 29)"}], "slide_number": 29, "section_ids": ["HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0029", "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-PART03", "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "HHS4867-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS4867 - Functional Movement Science", "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "Pathological gait", "Shuffling gait"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
