{"source_passage_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0031-PASSAGE", "text": "Trendelenburg Gait\nThe Trendelenburg gait occurs due to\nweakness of the hip abductor muscles\n(gluteus medius), primarily on the stance\nleg. This weakness prevents stabilization of\nthe pelvis during walking.\nThe commonest pattern consists of\n• Contralateral Pelvic Drop: During the • stance phase of the affected leg, the pelvis drops on the opposite (swing) side.\n• Lateral Trunk Lean (Compensation): • The patient leans their trunk laterally over the affected stance leg to shift their center of gravity and reduce the demand on weak abductors.", "document_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "document_title": "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "source_file": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0031"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0031", "document_id": "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "document_title": "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "source_file": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf", "page_number": 31, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 31, "pdf_page": 31, "formatted": "19 - 6. Postural and Gait 姿勢及步態評估.pdf, slide 31 (PDF p. 31)"}], "slide_number": 31, "section_ids": ["HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-P0031", "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT-PART03", "HHS4867-L06-POSTURAL-GAIT", "HHS4867-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS4867 - Functional Movement Science", "Lecture 6 - Postural Assessment and Gait", "Pathological gait", "Trendelenburg Gait"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
